1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Welcome to this practical review of reliable subtitle translation.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:25,000
We will compare several choices and explain why each one matters.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The first section introduces the problem in clear everyday language.

4
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Accurate timing keeps the translated text connected to the original speech.

5
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Long recordings are divided into independent requests for dependable processing.

6
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Each completed request should become visible without waiting for every other request.

7
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Temporary provider limits must not erase work that has already completed.

8
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Results still need to return in the same order as the source captions.

9
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The final section checks persistence, readability, and consistent presentation.

10
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:25,000
A relaunch should restore the exact translated track selected by the customer.

11
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:40,000
No successful segment should disappear because a neighboring request finishes later.

12
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:55,000
This closing caption confirms that the complete source range was preserved.
